# Architecture — {{.ProjectTitle}}

{{.Framework}} API on Node 24{{if .IsTypeScript}} (TypeScript, run directly with type stripping){{end}}. PostgreSQL 18 through
Drizzle (`pg` driver), Redis for refresh-token rotation and login rate limits, RS256 JWTs (`jose`).
The HTTP contract matches the Go templates (paths, envelopes, field names), so a frontend or BFF works with either.

## Request flow

```
HTTP → middleware (context, request log, security headers, CORS?, JSON body limit)
     → delivery/http (/v1/<domain>, authentication per group)
     → app/<domain>/<action> (parse + validate input)
     → service/<domain>/<method> (business rules, errors.*)
     → repository/<entity>/<method> (Drizzle via conn(ctx)) → PostgreSQL
     → repository/redis/* → Redis
```

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `src/main` | Startup: connect Redis + check DB (fail fast), listen, graceful shutdown |
| `src/app` | `createApp(factory)` — the app without listening (tests use it) |
| `src/config/config` | Environment variables validated by zod at import |
| `src/factory/factory` | Wires repositories, keys, trxManager; tests build their own with mocks |
| `src/delivery/http` | Group paths (`/v1/...`) and which groups need authentication |
| `src/middleware/*` | context, security headers, CORS, authentication, authorization (`requirePermission`, `requireRole`), request log, errors |
| `src/app/<domain>/*` | `handler`, `route` (relative paths), one file per action |
| `src/service/<domain>/*` | `service` (type + constructor), one file per method |
| `src/repository/<entity>/*` | The 12 standard methods, one file each (`user-role` / `role-permission` add assign/revoke/sync methods) |
| `src/repository/redis/*` | Refresh-token families (Lua CAS), rate-limit counters, permission cache (`authz:user:<id>`, `authz:role:<id>`) |
| `src/model/*` | Drizzle tables mirroring `migrations/`, `beforeCreate`/`beforeUpdate` hooks |
| `src/dto/*` | zod request schemas, filters + sort allowlists, response mappers |
| `src/abstraction/*` | Context, entity/audit helpers, pagination, errors, response envelopes, `parse` |
| `src/pkg/*` | database, redis, logger (pino), auth-token, password (bcrypt), trxmanager |
| `migrations/` | SQL source of truth (golang-migrate) |

## Endpoints

| Method | Path | Auth (permission held by one of the user's roles) |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/v1/health` | public |
| POST | `/v1/auth/login`, `/v1/auth/refresh`, `/v1/auth/logout` | public (refresh token in body for refresh/logout) |
| GET | `/v1/users/me` | access token |
| GET, PUT | `/v1/users/:id` | `users:read` / `users:update` |
| POST | `/v1/users` | `users:create` (the new user gets the `user` role) |
| PUT | `/v1/users/:id/roles` | `roles:manage` (replaces the user's roles) |
| GET, POST | `/v1/samples` | `samples:read` / `samples:create` |
| GET, PUT, DELETE | `/v1/samples/:id` | `samples:read` / `samples:update` / `samples:delete` (`:own` = only your rows) |
| GET, POST | `/v1/roles` | `roles:manage` |
| GET, PUT, DELETE | `/v1/roles/:id`, PUT `/v1/roles/:id/permissions` | `roles:manage` (`code` is immutable) |

API docs (outside `APP_ENV=production`): OpenAPI 3.1 at `/openapi.json`, Swagger UI at `/swagger/` (local
`swagger-ui-dist`, no CDN; its install-time analytics are disabled with `scarfSettings` in `package.json`). The
document is generated from the request zod schemas listed in `src/openapi/openapi.ts`. Responses are documented as the
generic `{ meta, data }` envelope (the `data` shape is not described); add a response schema per route if clients
generate code from the document.

`APP_BASE_PATH` (optional) prefixes every route when the API itself must serve under a path; usually the reverse
proxy adds the prefix instead.

## Testing

- `npm test`: unit + HTTP tests with mocked repositories (no database, no Redis).
- `npm run test:integration`: Redis Lua scripts and repositories against the local Docker services only
  (`make pg-start redis-start migrate-up`).
